.TH sync 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
sync \- flush the buffer cache to disc
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sync
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sync
writes out every modified block the kernel is holding, and returns when
the writes have been handed to the driver.
.SH OPTIONS
None.
.SH NOTES
The kernel writes buffers out as it goes, so
.B sync
is not needed routinely.  It matters before pulling the card out or
resetting the board by hand \-
.BR shutdown (1)
does it for you, and is the better habit.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR shutdown (1),
.BR umount (1),
.BR remount (1)
